// Regression: a slur must be RESERVED in the inter-staff gap. LilyPond's Slur is an
// ordinary inside-staff grob (no outside-staff-priority), so it joins the staff's vertical
// skyline like the clef and the tuplet bracket, and the staff below must clear its bow.
//
// Before this fixture existed the corpus saw it nowhere: SkylineBuilder had no "slur" in
// it, so a slur drooping into the gap was reserved nowhere and the staff below could settle
// onto it. SkylineBuilder.AddSlursToSkyline now seeds the flattened bow, from a staff-frame
// SlurLayout (MultiStaffLayouter.StaffSlurLayouts).
//
// The shape is the corpus books SD and SU (audit/lp-geometry/probes/page-vertical.ly),
// which pin the same geometry against real LilyPond: staff.staff.slur-under-notes and
// -over-notes. The pitches put the notes UNDER StaffGrouper's basic-distance of 9 while the
// slur's droop beats it, so the gap reads the slur and not the floor. Default slur
// direction: a low note takes an up stem so its slur curves down, and vice versa.
//
// Bar 1 hangs a DOWN slur off the upper staff into the gap; bar 2 raises an UP slur out of
// the lower staff into it — in different bars so the two bows never share an x.
octave absolute
time 8/4
key c major
title "Slurs reserve their room in the staff gap"
part rh { clef treble }
part lh { clef bass }
section S {
  rh {
    g,1( g,1) | b1 b1 |
  }
  lh {
    d,1 d,1 | f1( f1) |
  }
}
form main { S }
score main "slur-under-whole-notes" { grandStaff { staff rh staff lh } }
